 "evidence": "Two CM1 runs of the sea box's third lunar day from one restart, one realization each, which differ in the boundary-layer scheme's asymptotic length alone (453 and 75 m); domain diagnostics every 3 hours compared output for output, 3-D outputs every 6 hours, CM1's own flux diagnostics split by part. A sensitivity of CM1 to its own scheme on a 6 km grid, not a test of either length against observation.",
 "reading_rule": "days.quarters: by quarter of the lunar day (hour angle from noon), each run's means over the domain diagnostics both wrote: mixed_depth_km by pbl_mixing.rise_height from 0.314 km (0.5 K of virtual potential temperature), vapour_drop_g_kg the mixing ratio at 0.314 km less that at 6.201 km, lid_rise_k the virtual potential temperature at 8.238 km less that at 6.201 km (the GCM's full levels at the site), vapour_g_kg and theta_v_k at fixed heights, hpbl_km CM1's own depth, highest_cloud_km the highest level any column holds cloud; rain_mm_day at the ground from CM1's running totals; clouds: means over the 3-D outputs both wrote (6-hourly) of the share of columns holding cloud of 0.01 g/kg below 40 km, the median and 90th percentile of their highest cloudy level (m) and the share of all columns whose cloud reaches above 16 km; lid: box_lid's parts (W/m2, upward) averaged over 6.45 and 6.99 km, with the scheme's share and diffusivity. after_midnight: the verdict under criteria, set before the run. held_nights: the 6 km held nights' second day, both lengths.",
